1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,750
That pigeon isn't bobbing its head.

2
00:00:01,830 --> 00:00:02,270
Watch.

3
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:04,600
With every step, its head locks in place,

4
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,530
frozen in the air, while its body walks forward underneath.

5
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:09,420
Then the head snaps ahead to catch up,

6
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:10,350
and locks again.

7
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:11,510
Hold, snap.

8
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:12,410
Hold, snap.

9
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:12,970
Why?

10
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:14,920
A pigeon can barely move its eyes,

11
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,840
so it steadies its whole head instead,

12
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:18,470
like a camera on a tripod.

13
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:20,530
Every hold gives it a sharp,

14
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:22,380
still picture to spot seeds,

15
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:23,410
and hawks.

16
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:25,660
Scientists showed it with a treadmill.

17
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:28,760
When the world around the walking pigeon stopped moving,

18
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:29,990
so did the bobbing.

19
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:32,140
So next time one struts past you,

20
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:33,330
look closely, because
